Android P has public platform policy renamed, but neither for private policies, nor Android N policy.  A regression of CTS detected weird sets of allow rules, which was randomly created due to base_typeattr_XXX is the same between CrOS and Android policy. This change is to fix the regression.  BUG=b:80461815,b:112375461 TEST=sesearch -A -t app_data_file -p open -s cros_init  Change-Id: I0a78d7872ede1307f7ee6a32cf3704cb97793169 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/1168715 Commit-Ready: Kenny Root &lt;kroot@google.com&gt; Tested-by: Kenny Root &lt;kroot@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Kenny Root &lt;kroot@google.com&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="1168715" owner_email="fqj@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" ref="refs/changes/15/1168715/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ibb908a731d674db3a8e750dc8944c4826493fbe4" commit="442ed7f5d22f063d0716e425fd66807cfcb50e91" commit_message="diagnosis-tool: no space in object curly  Enforce the following format:    import {TestCase} from './interfaces/test-case';   const obj = {foo: 'FOO'};  BUG=b:111100698 TEST=ng lint TEST=ng lint diagnosis-tool --fix  Change-Id: Ibb908a731d674db3a8e750dc8944c4826493fbe4 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/1170672 Commit-Ready: Wei-Han Chen &lt;stimim@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Wei-Han Chen &lt;stimim@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Pi-Hsun Shih &lt;pihsun@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="1170672" owner_email="stimim@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/platform/factory" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/factory" ref="refs/changes/72/1170672/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-4.14" change_id="I0c5effbdd27ff593cc8799c6a7cd588b8cd715bd" commit="50fb5b89a8985d28ba1c04fff028de1822cde77f" commit_message="CHROMIUM: iwl7000: Merge Core35 driver updates  This is a merge commit of all Intel patches for the Core35 driver update since commit c055e9c0dcf22ecd67dfe5fef8388b7d981ba9fd and ending at commit 01a2c378bd85641f74e2a179e6654c77ed3e1991.  The original branch provided by Intel (Luca Coelho) is at branch core35-for-chromeos-4.14 on https://git.kernel.org/cgit/linux/kernel/git/iwlwifi/chromeos.git and has been mirrored as intel-wifi/v4.14-core35 on cros.  Below is the complete shortlog of all the merged patches: Avraham Stern (2):       CHROMIUM: iwl7000: mvm: Send LQ command as async when necessary       CHROMIUM: iwl7000: mvm: set wep key for all stations in soft ap mode  Colin Ian King (1):       CHROMIUM: iwl7000: mvm: remove division by size of sizeof(struct ieee80211_wmm_rule)  Dreyfuss, Haim (2):       CHROMIUM: iwl7000: mac80211: fix WMM TXOP calculation       CHROMIUM: iwl7000: chromeOS: add hard coded wmm rules if cfg80211 doesn't support it  Emmanuel Grumbach (8):       CHROMIUM: iwl7000: mvm: fix TSO with highly fragmented SKBs       CHROMIUM: iwl7000: mvm: fix a mixed declaration and code compilation problem       CHROMIUM: iwl7000: improve the flow when a NIC is disconnected       CHROMIUM: iwl7000: mvm: send BCAST management frames to the right station       CHROMIUM: iwl7000: mvm: honor the max_amsdu_subframes limit       CHROMIUM: iwl7000: mvm: clear HW_RESTART_REQUESTED when stopping the interface       CHROMIUM: iwl7000: dbg: don't crash if the firmware crashes in the middle of a debug dump       CHROMIUM: iwl7000: mac80211: fix a race between restart and CSA flows  Erel Geron (1):       CHROMIUM: iwl7000: fix non_shared_ant for 9000 devices  Golan Ben Ami (1):       CHROMIUM: iwl7000: pcie: fit reclaim msg to MAX_MSG_LEN  Gregory Greenman (1):       CHROMIUM: iwl7000: mvm: open BA session only when sta is authorized  Guenter Roeck (1):       CHROMIUM: iwl7000: chromeOS: Stop clogging kernel log with &quot;ETSI WMM data ...&quot;  Hao Wei Tee (1):       CHROMIUM: iwl7000: pcie: compare with number of IRQs requested for, not number of CPUs  Ido Yariv (2):       CHROMIUM: iwl7000: Add missing 11n disable module parameter check       CHROMIUM: iwl7000: mac80211: Fix skb overflow on association  Ihab Zhaika (2):       CHROMIUM: iwl7000: add killer cards for 9000 series       CHROMIUM: iwl7000: add new cards for 9000 and 22000 series  Ilan Peer (1):       CHROMIUM: iwl7000: mvm: Allow TKIP for AP mode  Johannes Berg (8):       CHROMIUM: iwl7000: chromeOS: use kernel version 99.0 for unreleased code       CHROMIUM: iwl7000: don't WARN on trying to dump dead firmware       CHROMIUM: iwl7000: mvm: fix race in queue notification wait       CHROMIUM: iwl7000: api: annotate compressed BA notif array sizes       CHROMIUM: iwl7000: fix LED command capability bit       CHROMIUM: iwl7000: cfg80211: remove division by size of sizeof(struct ieee80211_wmm_rule)       CHROMIUM: iwl7000: pcie: check iwl_pcie_txq_build_tfd() return value       CHROMIUM: iwl7000: chromeOS: fix subdir-ccflags-y usage  Luca Coelho (10):       CHROMIUM: iwl7000: mvm: fix old scan version sizes       CHROMIUM: iwl7000: mac80211: assign value to sband before accessing in ieee80211_config_bw()       CHROMIUM: iwl7000: chromeOS: 32 bit images are not supported in XVT       CHROMIUM: iwl7000: mvm: check for n_profiles validity in EWRD ACPI       CHROMIUM: iwl7000: fix vendor commands enumerations       Merge remote-tracking branch 'upstream/chromeos-4.14' into merge_4.14       CHROMIUM: iwl7000: chromeOS: Tweak backport headers for 4.4 support       CHROMIUM: iwl7000: chromeOS: ack that chromeos-4.4 supports NL80211_IFTYPE_NAN       CHROMIUM: iwl7000: chromeOS: don't backport nla_put_u64_64bit() for chromeos-4.4       Merge remote-tracking branch 'upstream/chromeos-4.14' into core35-for-chromeos-4.14  Matt Chen (1):       CHROMIUM: iwl7000: pcie: avoid unnecessary work if NIC is disconnected  Naftali Goldstein (2):       CHROMIUM: iwl7000: nvm: get num of hw addresses from firmware       CHROMIUM: iwl7000: nvm: fix warning in case fw declares no hw addresses  Rajat Jain (1):       CHROMIUM: iwl7000: pcie: Fail fast if HW is inaccessible at probe  Sara Sharon (6):       CHROMIUM: iwl7000: mvm: fix BAR seq ctrl reporting       CHROMIUM: iwl7000: mvm:  avoid sending too many BARs       CHROMIUM: iwl7000: pcie: set interrupt coalescing also for gen2       CHROMIUM: iwl7000: dbg: decrement occurrences for all triggers       CHROMIUM: iwl7000: pcie: fix RBDs ownership when moving to emergency       CHROMIUM: iwl7000: mvm: don't send keys when entering D3  Shaul Triebitz (2):       CHROMIUM: iwl7000: mvm: do not override amsdu size user settings       CHROMIUM: iwl7000: pcie: avoid empty free RB queue  Tova (1):       CHROMIUM: iwl7000: nvm: reduce warning visibility when no HW address is available  BUG=b:111819239 TEST=(TBD) wifi_matfunc/wifi_perf on grunt fitted with ThP2. Relaxing test failures on 4.14 only since - ThP2 is still in bring-up phase. Signed-off-by: Kirtika Ruchandani &lt;kirtika@chromium.org&gt;  Change-Id: I0c5effbdd27ff593cc8799c6a7cd588b8cd715bd Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/1154439 Commit-Ready: Kirtika Ruchandani &lt;kirtika@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Kirtika Ruchandani &lt;kirtika@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Kirtika Ruchandani &lt;kirtika@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="1154439" owner_email="kirtika@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/39/1154439/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ie36bb36b976d88d2a6b71fe562c7612e6a15664b" commit="d646f7cb7b7b42ffce8adfaa946f467826ff113d" commit_message="cros_component: manifest the gyp being no-op  The gyp file has been no-op. It only creates ninja files but nothing else. This change makes it explicit and stops to create the ninja files. cf. chromeos-common-script.gyp.  BUG=chromium:767517 TEST=cros_workon_make --board=eve cros_component --test TEST=precq  Change-Id: Ie36bb36b976d88d2a6b71fe562c7612e6a15664b Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/1148035 Commit-Ready: Keigo Oka &lt;oka@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Keigo Oka &lt;oka@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Keigo Oka &lt;oka@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="1148035" owner_email="oka@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/platform2" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform2" ref="refs/changes/35/1148035/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I0a6af2be7e544fd243670a8b6a06c2da6d23187f" commit="a8fb92230cc6a71ddbbf309dadfc077f37735225" commit_message="CRAS: cras_alsa_ucm - Support setting MinSoftwareGain value in UCM  Now we can set MinSoftwareGain after MaxSoftwareGain is set. It is used to limit the range of software gain.  When WebRTC uses headset mic, automatic gain control (AGC) may change the system gain. After removing headset mic, AGC can not understand and set it back if there is a large difference between internal mic and headset mic. If we keep software gain of internal mic always at the same value, we can solve this problem.  BUG=chromium:872192 TEST=Succussly set MinSoftwareGain on Coral board.  Change-Id: I0a6af2be7e544fd243670a8b6a06c2da6d23187f Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/1167010 Commit-Ready: Yu-Hsuan Hsu &lt;yuhsuan@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Yu-Hsuan Hsu &lt;yuhsuan@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Cheng-Yi Chiang &lt;cychiang@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="1167010" owner_email="yuhsuan@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="9" project="chromiumos/third_party/adhd" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/adhd" ref="refs/changes/10/1167010/9" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><lkgm version="10955.0.0-rc2"/></manifest>